": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua They have banned recreating games. They kinda suck for doing that.", "url": "https://x.com/J_N_Actual/status/2117333579650744710"}, {"author_id": "1396828125342969857", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:40:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117325998756868135"], "id": "2117325998756868135", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2084287702514417664", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117241485263298809", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@aijackass @kimmonismus @chetaslua Video gen via diffusion is super compute heavy. 15 seconds of high quality Seedance can cost like $10. This should be way more efficient. It’s not calculating pixel by pixel each frame", "url": "https://x.com/contentstrats/status/2117325998756868135"}, {"author_id": "1239501246035361792", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:36:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117325060453331351"], "id": "2117325060453331351", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua crazyyyy", "url": "https://x.com/la_bct/status/2117325060453331351"}, {"author_id": "1038159064088432640", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:35:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117324859021623454"], "id": "2117324859021623454", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 44, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua I hope this is not Fable 5.5 🤦‍♂️. It’s so over if it is", "url": "https://x.com/Azuchian1/status/2117324859021623454"}, {"author_id": "1544090025968766983", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:16:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117320023651831899"], "id": "2117320023651831899", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 292, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua Its not really video, its a lot like I did with Astra for a background in this video. Its more like a slide deck with motion graphics. If you try to duplicate what chetaslua did by asking it to create a video, your results will probably be varied and wild, no go back and ask it https://t.co/4Po3uA1Ehd", "url": "https://x.com/AphanFX/status/2117320023651831899"}, {"author_id": "1672477665482113024", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:13:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117319214373757205"], "id": "2117319214373757205", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 124, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua Oh I see sorry, they are saying this was done from a single prompt.  That is beyond Opus 5.5", "url": "https://x.com/J155886/status/2117319214373757205"}, {"author_id": "1818642541765705728", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:10:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117318412498272313"], "id": "2117318412498272313", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua oh this is the end of video generation tools sadly", "url": "https://x.com/itzKashan2912/status/2117318412498272313"}, {"author_id": "1860894065560027136", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:08:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117318029969387879"], "id": "2117318029969387879", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 183, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua I wonder if there is such a thing as creating libraries or even frameworks to improve the ability to create animations with pure code (to improve quality, consistency, and take less time and effort)", "url": "https://x.com/superlearners_/status/2117318029969387879"}, {"author_id": "2109949205246865408", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:07:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117317602544623979"], "id": "2117317602544623979", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 51, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua if it's truly pure code that's the real jump. we gave this exact prompt to the 4 models you can use today and 3 of them quietly called a video model and wrapped the mp4 😂 only gemini 4 argon wrote real code 👇 https://t.co/2QgJOuBUQE", "url": "https://x.com/evals_ag/status/2117317602544623979"}, {"author_id": "2116606539779710976", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:05:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117317097772728381"], "id": "2117317097772728381", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua Is release imminent?", "url": "https://x.com/SIMafiaBoss/status/2117317097772728381"}, {"author_id": "1904576168902483971", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:53:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117314243091657085"], "id": "2117314243091657085", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua making videos (shapes) isn’t a benchmark to see how good a model is", "url": "https://x.com/BlueCrystais/status/2117314243091657085"}, {"author_id": "2060020349258080256", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:49:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117313076517347520"], "id": "2117313076517347520", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua If this is true / not faked -- that's insane for it to be from pure code", "url": "https://x.com/Darkest_Rains/status/2117313076517347520"}, {"author_id": "1656510757213978626", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:46:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117312350244290718"], "id": "2117312350244290718", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 86, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua Increasingly looks like this earth might be a Fable 7 world", "url": "https://x.com/Emotelligent_AI/status/2117312350244290718"}, {"author_id": "18266407", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:32:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117309006049845622"], "id": "2117309006049845622", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 95, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua If that is pure code - insane progress ...", "url": "https://x.com/cmerk72/status/2117309006049845622"}, {"author_id": "1998083704405753856", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:03:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117301459419357547"], "id": "2117301459419357547", "in_reply_to_user_id": "823352160", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117272553500864731", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@BenjieMalinao That's the real test. It holds up much better if each scene is its own function with fixed start and end times, so \"change scene 3\" only touches one block. One giant file with shared state is where edits start breaking things two scenes later.", "url": "https://x.com/ellypromtstar/status/2117301459419357547"}, {"author_id": "1998083704405753856", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:02:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117301364535542173"], "id": "2117301364535542173", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1894589842040016896", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117292867555299407", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ProctoredGames Usually one big HTML file: a canvas or SVG scene, a few hundred lines of JS where every shape's position is a function of the frame number, and a tiny loop that steps frames. Then something like Puppeteer or HyperFrames screenshots each frame and ffmpeg stitches them. No assets,", "url": "https://x.com/ellypromtstar/status/2117301364535542173"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"author_id": "1573399256836309009", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:03:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117226039998906520"], "id": "2117226039998906520", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1017, "impression_count": 195032, "like_count": 4296, "quote_count": 40, "reply_count": 174, "retweet_count": 153}, "text": "This is most likely the latest Fable 5.5 checkpoint. The video is pure code.\n\nFable 5.5 will change the entire game. Im speechless. And yet, 99% of folks outside of our bubble have no idea.\n\nh/t @chetaslua  https://t.co/wjrevWnDDI"}, {"author_id": "1993270634080874496", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:06:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117226801298563255"], "id": "2117226801298563255", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 9376, "like_count": 54, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua i mean looks cool but their prove is basically screenshots and \"trust me bro\" - very simple to fake and opus 5.5 could create this with few prompts too. Kinda questionable if anthropic randomly giving fable 5.5 to people considering how scared they are of people misusing it +"}, {"author_id": "1010623768585211905", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:57:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117375644296257835"], "id": "2117375644296257835", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua @mjl11061"}, {"author_id": "2084287702514417664", "created_at": "2026-11-02T13:04:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117241485263298809"], "id": "2117241485263298809", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1527, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua But wouldn’t it use a lot more tokens to create this and code versus a video gen model?"}, {"author_id": "823352160", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:08:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117272553500864731"], "id": "2117272553500864731", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117226039998906520", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus @chetaslua cool demo but i want to see what happens when you ask it to change one scene in that file. generating it once is the fun part, editing it later is where i've watched models fall apart"}, {"author_id": "1894589842040016896", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:28:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117292867555299407"], "id": "2117292867555299407", "in_reply_to_user_id": "398680417", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117277020610789803", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@leohuanfang @kimmonismus @chetaslua What does the source code even look like for this? Im honestly curious"}], "users": [{"id": "1792690788326952960", "name": "Oskar", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 26, "following_count": 209, "like_count": 12314, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 4, "tweet_count": 143}, "username": "sooskars"}, {"id": "1106896608", "name": "Kirk Patrick Miller", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 15235, "following_count": 9699, "like_count": 202607, "listed_count": 177, "media_count": 11759, "tweet_count": 141474}, "username": "Chaos2Cured"}, {"id": "180848844", "name": "Bagdex", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1929, "following_count": 1081, "like_count": 14275, "listed_count": 13, "media_count": 